Z||000006||Fiero Heaven||03-02-2000||03:08 AM||||Hi Greg and ALL!<P>My apologies for not responding sooner, but give me a break, please!  I've been down the <BR>last week and a half with a wrenched back (from moving a Fiero, of course!), and not very able to deal with much of anything - especially wading through a couple hundred e-mails...<P>If you are nervous about your $50 deposit (which you suggested, in order to get in on the first build delivery), I'd be happy to return it.  No problem.<P>My HEADERS! builder has (once again) promised (that's why I told you I didn't want to commit to any delivery date), that he would have a Dyno-testable unit of our final design ready by the end of this week.  Well, I will certainly believe it, when I have it in my hot <BR>little hands!  We have arrangements ready and waiting (for a couple months, now!) for the Dyno shop, a test car, an installer (and a whole lot of interested Fiero Fans around the country - outside of the country, for that matter!).<P>Just as soon as we have Dyno results, EVERYONE who has already contacted us directly will be notified (to give them a few days advance notice), before posting it on all the Lists for everybody's evaluation.<P>I haven't been posting any updates because, like you, I have just been too disappointed by <BR>how long (and how much) all of this has taken.  It does seem that we are at long last getting close.  Please hang in there, if you can.  I really do expect them to be well worth the wait.  Thanks!<P>Looking forward to sharing the news as soon as we have it,<BR>Fiero Heaven<BR>John<P>||||reg||4
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||03-02-2000||09:02 AM||||Way COOL!!!!<P>We have the FieroHeaven man himself here in the forum.  <P>Absolutely (almost) everything fiero related is located here and that is very cool!||||reg||10
Z||000008||superXmotorsports||03-02-2000||07:57 PM||||Glad to see John hangs out in the forum too!  Must have been that threat of 800 emails!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't wish that on anyone. (well most people)<P>Good to hear that Fieroheaven is alive and well.  I will look forward to the headers on my 3.2L.  <P>I will continue to recommend the repro GT 1/4 windows (which are vg quailty) and the B&B exhaust system.  I just didn't want all the people I sent Fieroheaven's way to turn on me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>SXM.<P>||||reg||14
